cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dot-claude-iff, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "dot-claude-iff: a harness for human and agent collaboration in Claude Code, built on shared mental memory, collaborative handoff, and self-evolving ritual"
abstract: >-
  A generalizable .claude/ operating system that a repository adopts as a drop-in: a journal
  and its projections for session continuity, fail-closed gates (a policy gate on every write
  lane, a validator on every structured write), an out-of-repo record of every session, a
  user-only end-of-session ritual that regenerates every derived surface, a live console, and
  modes for solo and orchestrated work (a lead with builders in git worktrees). Hooks and tools
  are bash and Python standard library only.
authors:
